[section_header] b.   Insurance Ombudsman-
[list_item] The Ombudsman shall receive and consider complaints alleging deficiency in performance required of an insurer (including its agents and intermediaries) or an insurance broker, on any of the following grounds-
[list_item] (a) delay in settlement of claims, beyond the time specified in the regulations, framed under the Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority of India Act, 1999;
[list_item] (b) any partial or total repudiation of claims by the life insurer, general insurer or the health insurer;
[list_item] (c) disputes over Premium paid or payable in terms of insurance Policy;
[list_item] (d) misrepresentation of Policy terms and conditions at any time in the Policy document or Policy contract;
[list_item] (e) legal construction of insurance policies in so far as the dispute relates to claim;
[list_item] (f) Policy servicing related grievances against insurers and their agents and intermediaries;
[list_item] (g) issuance  of  life  insurance  Policy,  general  insurance  Policy  including  health  insurance  Policy  which  is  not  in conformity with the proposal form submitted by the proposer;
[list_item] (h) non-issuance of insurance Policy after receipt of Premium in life insurance and general insurance including health insurance; and
[list_item] (i) any other matter arising from non-observance of or non-adherence to the provisions of any regulations made by the Authority with regard to protection of policyholders' interests or otherwise, or of any circular, guideline or instruction issued by the Authority, or of the terms and conditions of the policy contract, insofar as such matter relates to issues referred to in clauses (a) to (h).
[section_header] c. Manner in which complaint is to be made -
[list_item] Any person who has a grievance against an insurer or insurance broker, may himself or through his legal heirs, nominee  or  assignee,  make  a  complaint  in  writing  to  the  Insurance  Ombudsman  within  whose  territorial jurisdiction the branch or office of the insurer or the insurance broker, as the case may be, complained against or the residential address or place of residence of the complainant is located.
[list_item] The complaint shall be in writing, duly signed or made by way of electronic mail or online through the website of the Council for Insurance Ombudsmen, by the complainant or through his legal heirs, nominee or assignee and shall state clearly the name and address of the complainant, the name of the branch or office of the insurer against whom the complaint is made, the facts giving rise to the complaint, supported by documents, the nature and extent of the loss caused to the complainant and the relief sought from the Insurance Ombudsman.
[list_item] No complaint to the Insurance Ombudsman shall lie unless-
[list_item] (a) the complainant has made a representation in writing or through electronic mail or online through website of the insurer  or  insurance  broker  concerned  to  the  insurer  or  insurance  broker,  as  the  case  may  be,  named  in  the complaint and-
[list_item] either the insurer or insurance broker, as the case may be, had rejected the complaint; or
[list_item] the complainant had not received any reply within a period of one month after the insurer or insurance broker, as the case may be, received his representation; or
